{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen","id":786503,"title":"How common was teaching House Lore among Fallen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-14T21:53:30-08:00","id":786503,"title":"How common was teaching House Lore among Fallen?","content":"The Fallen are said to have shared Lore back during the War of Wrath. Which Lore was likely the most commonly shared? I can easily see Lore of Celestials being taught up to the third level, and probably everyone knew the first dot of Lore of the Forge so they could help with creating Relics. Lore of Awakening was probably taught in full to every Fallen who wanted to learn, if only by a large minority of Scourges who wanted to make sure that healing magic would always be available to humanity as long as a Fallen was nearby. Lore of Portals at 3 or even 5 and Lore of Paths at 2 or perhaps even 3 or 4 was probably quite commonly learned once the war turned ugly and the Fallen began to rack up casualties, particularly once the Malhim took the field. Lore of Realms probably wasn't shared much, perhaps not at all, due to the circumstances surrounding that Lore. What other House Lore was likely passed around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T05:11:23-08:00","id":786653,"title":"","content":"I don't know how involved humanity really were in the war, but if the Elohim was in the habit of keeping close track then I could see Lore of the Firmament being passed around here and there; possibly Lore of Longing too for those who wanted to focus more on babysitting than fighting their kin on the other side of the conflict. Depending on how it played out I could see Lore of Longing being some sort of pre-cursor to Lore of Humanity even, though that's mostly speculations. The final Lore I could see a lot of use for with the Fallen's goals back in the days is the Lore of Flesh as it allows both healing and improvements when used properly.<br /> As a majority however, I don't think they flinged the secrets of each other's Lores around too much given the focus of warfare but rather relied on the members of whatever House normally possessed when and perhaps occasionally picked something up along the way or shared one or two tricks with a fellow rebel they grew attached to. Once again this is my &quot;only speculation&quot; grain of salt coming into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T09:33:14-08:00","id":786755,"title":"","content":"Sounds about right, though I would imagine there were probably a few bleeding heart Scourges who tried to foist their ability to heal and even bring humans back from the dead on other Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:39:59-08:00","id":786862,"title":"","content":"The rebels of the first house sharing their knowledge of the building blocks of reality with the lowly rabble? Please.<br /> <br /> Honestly learning lore is a very involved process (or should be at least). Demons are what they eat so to speak. They don't simply have lores, they embody them. So learning new lores is pretty hard and sharing with someone else is sharing part of your own very being, a statement of trust if there ever was one. So personally I assume that if someone learned out of house lores at all, then he either had a very close ally (or lover) from the other house or was of high(ish) rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:42:05-08:00","id":786957,"title":"","content":"Or had a captured angel imprisoned in his layer, or the knowledge trickled out from someone who did. Remember, most Fallen at first might have been too civilized to torture or devour Angels, but as the war dragged on they probably became less horrified at the prospect of putting pressure on someone who already did the dirty work. Even heaven possibly tortured the Lore of Realms out of a Fallen who knew it. <br /> <br /> Still, you are probably right that there are some major complications with demons learning Lore back then. If a Rabisu ate an angel of the First House or tortured knowledge out of it, it would probably be late in the war before it would be safe for that Rabisu to openly teach Lore of Flames or Celestials to his friends, even if he is trying to just give them the means to stay alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:48:08-08:00","id":786965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=786957#post786957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or had a captured angel imprisoned in his layer, or the knowledge trickled out from someone who did. Remember, most Fallen at first might have been too civilized to torture or devour Angels, but as the war dragged on they probably became less horrified at the prospect of putting pressure on someone who already did the dirty work. Even heaven possibly tortured the Lore of Realms out of a Fallen who knew it.<br /> <br /> Still, you are probably right that there are some major complications with demons learning Lore back then. If a Rabisu ate an angel of the First House or tortured knowledge out of it, it would probably be late in the war before it would be safe for that Rabisu to openly teach Lore of Flames or Celestials to his friends, even if he is trying to just give them the means to stay alive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think an elohim that tried torture would find itself rejected and falling to earth fast than it could say &quot;Good intentions&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T15:21:38-08:00","id":786985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=786965#post786965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think an elohim that tried torture would find itself rejected and falling to earth fast than it could say &amp;quot;Good intentions&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not. The Angels that sided with heaven seemed to have a &quot;just following orders&quot; and &quot;Napoleon/Michael/God is always right&quot; mentality. Remember how it was written in (Earthbound?) that Lucifer got to watch the Heavenly Host treat the humans on Earth like an occupying army would, roasting some and sparing others? Remember what type of orders they were willing to stand behind? And remember how ugly things got for them with the Ebon and Silver Legions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:51:58-08:00","id":787032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=786862#post786862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rebels of the first house sharing their knowledge of the building blocks of reality with the lowly rabble? Please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that's exactly how oWoD Mages came about, curtesy of Lucifer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T01:18:47-08:00","id":787208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=786985#post786985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not. The Angels that sided with heaven seemed to have a &quot;just following orders&quot; and &quot;Napoleon/Michael/God is always right&quot; mentality. Remember how it was written in (Earthbound?) that Lucifer got to watch the Heavenly Host treat the humans on Earth like an occupying army would, roasting some and sparing others? Remember what type of orders they were willing to stand behind? And remember how ugly things got for them with the Ebon and Silver Legions?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were very few non rebel Elohim who did so. The only concrete example I can remember is Usiel, who promptly got kicked into the abyss along with the rebels. The loyalists treated humanity more like cattle insofar as they took away Lucifers gift of cognition from them, turning them into little more than animals comprehensionwise (at least early in the war).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=786957#post786957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or had a captured angel imprisoned in his layer, or the knowledge trickled out from someone who did. Remember, most Fallen at first might have been too civilized to torture or devour Angels, but as the war dragged on they probably became less horrified at the prospect of putting pressure on someone who already did the dirty work.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though angels who frequently managed to bring down other angels (whether they devoured them or not) also tended to climb in rank to a degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only that's exactly how oWoD Mages came about, curtesy of Lucifer. </div> </div> </div>Not quite as far as I understood it. Mages were created by the bits and pieces of destroyed angels (not all of them were devoured, some just torn apart) latching onto human souls. It had nothing to do with teaching them how to use lores, though I could Lucifer see help them develop their powers. What Lucifer teached humanity were the basics of sorcery, so they could summon the others from the abyss. But even then Lucifer is a very far cry from most devils personality wise. Or rather he fits his house by embodying an ideal, but not one I see commonly shared in fluff (except by hardcore Luciferans, over half of which are really just Lulu fanboys).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 12-16-2015, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T17:57:10-08:00","id":787742,"title":"","content":"I would say they shared their lores with those they worked closely with before the war and afterwards those in close military units most likely shared lores","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T21:05:36-08:00","id":787828,"title":"","content":"Makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T10:47:31-08:00","id":788207,"title":"","content":"In the Demon books Mages were specifically mentioned as being the result of the Babylon Project. I suspect that the Watchers may have some how acted as communal Avatars. After the war humanity may have adapted in ways that they didn't understand as the Angel pieces were floating around and may have latched on to mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T14:16:56-08:00","id":788959,"title":"","content":"I doubt that the Loyalists got nearly a fraction of the flexibility of the Fallen. It is every time and again said as the weapon of demons to fight against the odds. So I doubt that a loyalist would learn anything outside her House, or had the need to learn inside it. They probably didn't had even Rituals as the Fallen came to understand them, nor learned the new Lores of the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Just remember that they had numbers (2 loyalists for every fallen just to begin with, Heaven knows what else God was creating to support its legions) and access to an infinite source of Faith (God itself), so energy wasn't an issue not even for the most powerful uses.<br /> <br /> How much Lore the Fallen actually shared is hard to grasp, and actually irrelevant for almost all purposes. Sometimes they shared because they needed, and that is clear, as is that they altered their Lores to some degree (loyalists probably didn't had High Torment versions). It is also clear that they are fairly defined by nature, enough to justify a modern Fallen never relearning an out-of-house Lore she once possessed.<br /> <br /> Some were certainly forced by circumstances to share against their wills. And that can happen again. But for me, at least, it seems that most (not all) Fallen were far more open to share with their peers in the past than they are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T23:08:14-08:00","id":789126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=788959#post788959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But for me, at least, it seems that most (not all) Fallen were far more open to share with their peers in the past than they are now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The fallen have never been more handicapped, outgunned or had such an array of enemies against them as they do now. Lore is really about the only thing they have going for them. Back during the war there might have been some who could initially believe they didn't need to share, but the modern Fallen are really gimped and the way they are being forced to live is best described as &quot;undignified.&quot; They may demand favors before sharing their knowledge, but as they grasp just how big the WoD is and how small their kind has become they will accept that they will have to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T06:50:06-08:00","id":789231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=789126#post789126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. The fallen have never been more handicapped, outgunned or had such an array of enemies against them as they do now. Lore is really about the only thing they have going for them. Back during the war there might have been some who could initially believe they didn't need to share, but the modern Fallen are really gimped and the way they are being forced to live is best described as &quot;undignified.&quot; They may demand favors before sharing their knowledge, but as they grasp just how big the WoD is and how small their kind has become they will accept that they will have to share.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem I see with this thought is that it is too logical. Many of the fallen would much rather see all of their kind destroyed(themselves included) than even Admit that they aren't the masters of the universe anymore(that's doubly true for the earthbound in particular). Let alone Share knowledge with many they consider either their sworn enemies or beneath their notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:35:28-08:00","id":789306,"title":"","content":"Not to say those individuals don't exist, but don't you find the statement a bit too broad to be reasonable? Not every Fallen are that vain and illogical anymore than every American is a redneck Trump supporter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:51:57-08:00","id":789378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=789306#post789306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to say those individuals don't exist, but don't you find the statement a bit too broad to be reasonable? Not every Fallen are that vain and illogical anymore than every American is a redneck Trump supporter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand that my statement is very broad and won't fit with all demons, but since most demons are either mid-high torment or are subservient to a demon who is, they really don't have the liberty to make that choice.<br /> <br /> To a higher torment demon(whether their skewed worldview is rooted in pride, paranoia, or an alien form of logic) having you or your subordinates share lores either gives parties other than you a definite edge you can't risk, is an act of lowering yourself to someone else, or creates potential threats the have yet to be realized, so it really wouldn't appeal to their twisted minds.<br /> <br /> P.S. what I meant only really applies to a limited number of NPC's as the players aren't typically exposed to all the demons in wod and the ones they do will be far more likely to share because of the PCs tendency towards Main Character status(as most other types of NPCs would be antagonists)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T13:01:14-08:00","id":789391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=789378#post789378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. what I meant only really applies to a limited number of NPC's as the players aren't typically exposed to all the demons in wod and the ones they do will be far more likely to share because of the PCs tendency towards Main Character status(as most other types of NPCs would be antagonists)</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:27:35-08:00","id":789466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786503-how-common-was-teaching-house-lore-among-fallen?p=789126#post789126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. The fallen have never been more handicapped, outgunned or had such an array of enemies against them as they do now. Lore is really about the only thing they have going for them. Back during the war there might have been some who could initially believe they didn't need to share, but the modern Fallen are really gimped and the way they are being forced to live is best described as &quot;undignified.&quot; They may demand favors before sharing their knowledge, but as they grasp just how big the WoD is and how small their kind has become they will accept that they will have to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite true, to begin with.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the Fallen are weaker now than ever, and surrounded by dangers. But before they were at war with Heaven. That means that they were facing a force with more than two times their size and infinite basic resource (Faith). It was a dire circumstance, far more objectively dangerous than their current state. They were <u><b>definitely</b></u> more outgunned back them!<br /> <br /> Also, you completely ignores the canon description of their moral at the time. At the beginning of the War, they were Angels to all ethical and emotional purposes in their way to deal with each other. Some already manifested traits that would later make them into monsters, but in this stage they are the most cooperative beings in the universe, or close enough to it. Maybe they had natural resistance to share Lore when it was like sharing purpose in the universe, but they were more wiling to do things simply for a common cause. They were far more selfless.<br /> <br /> Then you have the other way around. Today they are in a weakened state. But they're also at odds against themselves. From all potential enemies for a Demon, the most probable to do greater harm in the long term is another Demon. Physical bodies are just a commodity, time is plentiful for them even more than for Vampires. Against almost anyone a Demon can think in the long run and see its own demise as just a little hindrance in the way. But other Demons can fool it for more time, they can face it again and again, and they already know more about it and how to deal with it than any other splat. They are far more selfish now, but above that, they're far more paranoid.<br /> <br /> Back in the beginning of the war, sharing was against their pride. But now it is against survival. Yes, they need to learn to survive, but they also need their enemies not to learn. And they don't even know who among them will be an enemy in the future.<br /> <br /> You can also add simple military order. In a war, you follow any order given by a superior. The legions of the Fallen weren't as organized as not to have contentions, but in any given platoon it is to expect that a commander had almost complete authority over its subordinates. So sometimes the trade of Lores was simply commanded from above, and the process regulated by militaristic efficiency. The modern hellish courts aren't armies, they don't have reason or means to ensure or follow military rank and obedience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T22:54:13-08:00","id":789619,"title":"","content":"These are all good points, but I think you need to look at the way they have been steadily shaped since the Fall. Before the Fall no Angel would be caught dead sharing their House's precious Lore. Even after the Fall they were extremely reluctant and apparently didn't even really begin to at all until the war was really under way, and even then it was just a few tricks. That was back when they could each sunder mountains or boil oceans with a wave of their hands. <br /> <br /> Now, they are weaker and suffering more indignities than they could ever have imagined themselves to be. Once sharing your House's Lore with outsiders might have been the ultimate taboo, but the Fallen just aren't in a position to be fussy anymore. They now need to eat, pay for shelter, possibly support others, find a way to get around and so on. Hell, in the fiction I think one or two were even living on the streets. This may not make your average demon feel generous, but when you've got them living like Castiel or Metatron in Supernatural did back when they were human they are definitely going to be hungry for power. If they aren't prepared to canabalise for it they will likely be open to making a trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:55:05-08:00","id":793599,"title":"","content":"I do myself play with a Fallen that is completely homeless and broken, to the point of eating leftovers from thrash cans. You are right about their current predicament. But their previous one were as dire, if in another way, or worse. And without more sharing than you ascribe to them, they wouldn't survive so much time as the war lasted, they would be in their knees in less than a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}